    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The open file. On POSIX each read is one pread, which keeps no file position, so a cache miss costs one system call instead of the seek and read an ifstream makes. With many threads reading at once those extra seeks added up to most of the run time. Closed by its destructor, so a <ref refid="classSpiceQL_1_1daf_1_1File" kindref="compound">File</ref> that fails to construct doesn&apos;t leak it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
